<title>USA: The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</title>
<headline>The top 10 movies at the U.S. box office.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following were the top 10 movies at the U.S. box office for the April 25-27 weekend, according to studio estimates collected on Sunday by Exhibitor Relations Co. Inc. Final numbers will be issued on Monday.</p>
<p>    1 (*) Volcano ..................... $14.7 million</p>
<p>    2 (*) Romy and Michelle's High</p>
<p>	    School Reunion ..............  $7.6 million</p>
<p>    3 (1) Anaconda ....................  $7.3 million</p>
<p>    4 (2) Liar Liar ...................  $6.8 million</p>
<p>    5 (4) The Saint ...................  $5.0 million</p>
<p>    6 (3) Murder At 1600 ..............  $4.7 million</p>
<p>    7 (5) Grosse Pointe Blank .........  $3.0 million</p>
<p>    8(11) Scream ......................  $1.4 million</p>
<p>    9 (6) The Devil's Own .............  $1.2 million</p>
<p>   10=(10)Chasing Amy .................  $1.1 million</p>
<p>   10=(8) That Old Feeling ............  $1.1 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Last weekend's position in parenthesis. * = new release.</p>
<p>&quot;Volcano&quot; is released by 20th Century Fox, a unit of News Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Romy and Michelle's High School Reunion&quot; and &quot;Grosse Pointe Blank&quot; are released by Walt Disney Co. &quot;Chasing Amy&quot; and &quot;Scream&quot; are released by Disney's Miramax Films.</p>
<p>&quot;Anaconda&quot; and &quot;The Devil's Own&quot; are released by Sony Corp..</p>
<p>&quot;Liar Liar&quot; and &quot;That Old Feeling&quot; are released by Universal Pictures, a unit of Seagram Co. Ltd..</p>
<p>&quot;The Saint&quot; is released by Paramount Pictures, a unit of Viacom Inc..</p>
<p>&quot;Murder at 1600&quot; is released by Warner Bros., a unit of Time Warner Inc..</p>
